# Tables: Break on a body Row forces a page break before it, or keeps two rows on the same page.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Tables · Breaks between rows
	Page:
		Paper: A5
		Margin: 15mm
	Styles:
		For element: Cell
			Box:
				Border: 0 0 0.5 0
				Border color: rule
		For element: Header cell
			Typography:
				Bold: true
		For style: group
			Typography:
				Bold: true
				Color: accent
			Box:
				Background: tint
	Section:
		Text: Tables
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Breaks between rows
		Paragraph: A body `Row` accepts `Break`, which is that of its cells. `Before: page` starts the row on a new page, with the header repeated. `Keep with next: true` keeps a group title with the row below it. A cell does not accept `Break`.
			Style: intro
		Table:
			Column sizes: * 70
			Column align: left right
			Header rows:
				Row:
					Cell: Product
					Cell: Price
			Body rows:
				Row:
					Style: group
					Break:
						Keep with next: true
					Cell: Chairs (Keep with next: true)
						Span: 1 2
				Row:
					Cell: Walnut chair
					Cell: 145.00
				Row:
					Cell: Oak chair
					Cell: 130.00
				Row:
					Style: group
					Break:
						Before: page
						Keep with next: true
					Cell: Tables (Before: page, Keep with next: true)
						Span: 1 2
				Row:
					Cell: Dining table
					Cell: 890.00
				Row:
					Cell: Coffee table
					Cell: 320.00
